  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 302 AM CDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nRidging takes hold again in the wake of the shortwave Wednesday, and \na slightly tighter pressure gradient enhances surface WAA out of the \nsouth. Highs will once again reach the upper 70s to around 80 \nWednesday and Thursday with mostly clear skies.\n\nA weak frontal boundary may support low rain chances for \nnorthern/central Missouri Thursday evening, which could sag \nsouthward and begin to affect the northern portions of the SGF CWA. \nAnother shortwave continues the train of shortwaves Friday, and rain \nchances look to exist over an extended period of time as waves of \nsupport pass through. Current timing shows widespread chances \nholding off until Saturday, with 40-60% PoPs area-wide. The NBM has \nbeen disagreeing with itself run-to-run, lowering and then raising \nprecipitation potential again, but the general consensus lands \naround those probabilities. CAPE will be quite low, and this \nrain should feel like a gentle, seasonal type of event. Rain \nchances linger into Sunday and potentially increase again to \nstart next week.\n\nLong-term models depict a deeper, more dynamic system dropping \nsoutheast through the area, bringing more rain to start\nNovember.",
